NEXT TEST: Test 1, run 8: DM + player script, player stops, on Deepgram
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why
  Run 7 gave the Deepgram baseline with the DM alone (33/33, 10/12). Still open: a
  scored run with two speakers, a player stopping mid-session, and a player getting
  the first-time question.

Where it runs
  Cloud test server, Docker Compose (postgres, core, ears), development branch,
  TRANSCRIBER=deepgram (nova-3), DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1. Server session watches logs.

Before the test (owner)
  [ ] Tell the server session how many people (1 = DM only, 2 = DM + player, ...)
      and send the matching script from docs/test-scripts/ (paste it into Discord)
  [ ] Someone who has NOT agreed before (ideally a third account) in voice before
      /dmbot start, for the first-time question
  [ ] Run /dmbot commands from any channel EXCEPT #dmb-transcript-... (they hang
      there: #188)
  [ ] Everyone presses I consent in DMbot's private message (or /consent give) BEFORE
      speaking; the player will be asked once more (new wording, names Deepgram)
  [ ] At each (( dramatic pause )): mute, count to three, unmute
  [ ] Note: packet loss tool on/off, each reader's Discord noise suppression

What to check
  - The player's request names Deepgram; capture starts only after their yes
  - Lines appear in #dmb-transcript-... a few seconds after speaking, labelled per
    speaker; the DM screen stays quiet
  - Stop recording me -> no more lines from that player in the transcript channel
  - Wait for the script's last line in the transcript channel before /dmbot stop
  - Score it (docs/test-scripts/README.md): audio from ears lines, pieces of speech,
    Part 1 of 35 (dm-and-player) or 33 (dm-only), Part 2 of 12, whisper, first word
    after each split pause (#121)
  - Compare with run 7 (Deepgram, DM only: 33/33, 10/12, whisper part) and run 6
    (local Whisper small: 33/33, 7/12, whisper all)

LATER TESTS
